Structure and Markdown (must follow):
- Section titles: `##` only (one level; avoid `###` subsections)
- Default writing unit: markdown bullets (`- item`) or numbered lists — not paragraphs
- Prose budget: at most 1–2 short sentences under a heading before switching to bullets or a table
- Comparisons, inventories, metrics, options: GFM pipe tables (≤5 columns; concise cells)
- Workflows, pipelines, architecture flows: fenced ```mermaid blocks (flowchart, sequenceDiagram, or graph) when evidence supports it
- Code, configs, commands, paths: fenced code blocks with a language tag when known
- If a point needs more than ~40 words, split it into bullets or a table row
- Skip empty sections; do not pad with filler prose
- Exception: when report style is `content_draft`, short paragraphs are OK for narrative body; still use a `##` outline and bullets for lists. All other styles: bullets and tables first.

